    "status": "present",
    "value": "Evaluate an expression in a tiny Lisp-like language and return its integer value. An expression is an integer, a variable name, or a parenthesised form: (add e1 e2) and (mult e1 e2) return the sum and product of their two operands; (let v1 e1 v2 e2 ... vn en body) assigns each variable in order (each expression may use variables assigned before it) and then returns the value of body. Variables are looked up in the innermost enclosing scope that defines them; a let's assignments disappear when the let ends. Tokens are separated by single spaces."
  },
